# Cursor IDE Rules for Android-MCP (android-as-a-tool)

# 1. Single Source of Truth
Mandatory review before modifying code or architecture:
- AGENTS.md: Quality directives, two-phase protocol (Gate 1 "Optimal & Acceptable", Gate 2 "Well-Crafted"), and security rules.
- RELEASE.md: Branching strategy, release checklist, and tag registry.

# 2. Android & ADB Security
- Never expose ADB port 5555 to public interfaces.
- Validate sources in install_apk against SSRF attacks (prohibit access to 169.254.169.254 or unauthorized private networks).
- Enforce PII sanitization when reading notifications (guardrails/input-guards.yaml).
- Prohibit bare `except Exception: pass` suppression; handle specific exceptions defensively.

# 3. LLM Token Efficiency
- Prioritize UIParser to retrieve compact interactive elements with (cx, cy) centroids over heavy screenshots.
- Maintain test suite (`python -m pytest`) and evaluation benchmarks at 100% pass rate.
